{"entryId":"3370","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3370:1","sourceSha256":"abd2f0e59fa6a50d0148f8f4312abb251204a3728b85ad6b1bfc80589ef91f3c","englishSha256":"56a7373201dbdd36826ccb30cad4e47d5f2d5663e45892ba431d3cce844ac7b8","citations":[{"id":"3370:1:link-006","he":[157,169],"en":[328,338],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_25b.9"},"reference":"Niddah 25b:9","assessment":"The account reports the forty-one-day estimate, the forty days counted from immersion, and the confession. Both consecutive segments were checked.","evidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 25b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_25b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Niddah 25b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_25b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-007","he":[198,214],"en":[378,389],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_102a.12"},"reference":"Eruvin 102a:12","assessment":"The exact source attributes the larger mortar and ruling about putting it against the door to Mar Shmuel.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eruvin 102a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_102a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-008","he":[293,307],"en":[534,545],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_55a.5"},"reference":"Nedarim 55a:5","assessment":"The primary witness gives thirteen thousand zuz and names Rava. A separate gloss in Heilprin 3337 gives twelve thousand.","evidence":[{"reference":"Nedarim 55a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_55a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3337:1","target":{"entry":3337,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-009","he":[378,410],"en":[686,697],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_34a.5"},"reference":"Menachot 34a:5","assessment":"The actual visit of Rav Pappa to Mar Shmuel concerned a doorway with a single doorpost and a mezuzah.","evidence":[{"reference":"Menachot 34a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_34a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-010","he":[451,464],"en":[778,789],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_14b.2"},"reference":"Beitzah 14b:2","assessment":"The checked folio gives Rav Pappi, the uneaten porridge, and a reason concerning the servants. This is a separate visitor occurrence from the one in Menahot.","evidence":[{"reference":"Beitzah 14b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_14b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Beitzah 14b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_14b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-011","he":[581,618],"en":[1060,1070],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_21b.11"},"reference":"Beitzah 21b:11","assessment":"Beitzah preserves the attribution formula and the ruling on inviting a gentile on the Sabbath and a festival. Its following rule distinguishes inviting a gentile on Sabbath from doing so on a festival.","evidence":[{"reference":"Beitzah 21b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_21b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-014","he":[309,341],"en":[547,594],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_16b.9"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 16b:9","assessment":"The Bavli names no father and specifies that he served among the scribes of Mar Shmuel’s court. Other Heilprin entries expose the disputed Yaakov/Yitzhak identification.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 16b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_16b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2114:1","target":{"entry":2114,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 2678:2","target":{"entry":2678,"paragraph":2},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-015","he":[343,376],"en":[595,656],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_25b.11"},"reference":"Beitzah 25b:11","assessment":"Beitzah gives an explicit first-person statement by Rav Naḥman bar Yitzhak that he moved Mar Shmuel from sun to shade and back.","evidence":[{"reference":"Beitzah 25b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_25b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3370:1:link-016","he":[474,498],"en":[807,839],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_19a.3"},"reference":"Berakhot 19a:3","assessment":"The checked Bavli directly contains the reed story and the answer regarding the honor of scholars.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 19a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_19a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Berakhot 19a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_19a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,6,7,3,4,8,5],"holds":[{"raw":"נראה כי היה ראש גולה","reason":"The exilarch identification is Heilprin’s conjecture. The checked story concerning the servants supplies no title.","evidence":[{"reference":"Beitzah 14b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_14b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The checked Beitzah names Rav Pappi. The preceding Menahot episode names Rav Pappa.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"In Bava Metzia 16b:9, Rav Naḥman says that his father was one of the scribes of Mar Shmuel’s court. The passage supplies no given name. Heilprin discusses the competing Yaakov and Yitzhak identifications in entries 2114 and 2678.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Beitzah 25b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_25b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
